WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.724
Libraries such as i18next and
next-intl display translations

2
00:00:04.724 --> 00:00:06.755
you supply in a file per language.

3
00:00:07.155 --> 00:00:09.082
They are mature and free,

4
00:00:09.082 --> 00:00:10.801
and they format plurals,

5
00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:13.214
dates, and numbers for each locale.

6
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.589
General Translation
does the same job,

7
00:00:15.589 --> 00:00:17.190
and also does the translating.

8
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.438
Your team writes copy inline,

9
00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:21.946
inside a T component.

10
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.563
Then npx gt translate writes
every target locale as a build

11
00:00:26.563 --> 00:00:27.038
step.

12
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.820
Or keep i18next or next-intl,

13
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.907
and let the gt CLI
translate their files.

14
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.377
Your team now ships
Japanese with each release.
